# Every change gets a review from the maintainers.
#
# The rule registry, the generated data and the published surfaces are called
# out separately - not because they need a different reviewer, but because a
# change to one of them is a change to what every consumer sees, and the file
# list on the pull request is where that is easiest to notice.

*                               @abap2UI5/maintainers

# The rule set: a new id, a changed severity or a reworded message reaches the
# CLI, the VS Code extension, mcp-server and samples-controls' gate policy.
/lib/findings.mjs               @abap2UI5/maintainers
/lib/rule-docs.mjs              @abap2UI5/maintainers

# Generated - never hand-edited. A diff here that is not the output of its
# generator is the thing to catch.
/data/                          @abap2UI5/maintainers
/site/                          @abap2UI5/maintainers

# The published contract: the exports map, the typings, the composite action.
/package.json                   @abap2UI5/maintainers
/types.d.ts                     @abap2UI5/maintainers
/action.yml                     @abap2UI5/maintainers

# CI, the release path and the OIDC publishing identity.
/.github/                       @abap2UI5/maintainers
